    <div class="card-header fw-semibold"><i class="bi bi-code-slash me-1"></i>REST API</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p>DashDDI exposes a REST API covering all major resources — hosts, interfaces, subnets, domains, records, and more. Interactive API documentation with request/response schemas and the ability to test calls is available at <a href="{{ path('api_docs') }}"><strong>API Docs</strong></a>.</p>
        <p>Authentication uses Bearer tokens. Create a token under <strong>Other Settings → API Tokens</strong> and grant only the per-route permissions that integration needs.</p>
        <p class="mb-0 text-muted small">The repository also includes a <strong>certbot-dns-dashddi</strong> Python plugin that enables Let's Encrypt DNS-01 challenge automation via DashDDI's API.</p>
